  "description": "Native rules for Skill Lab champions. Isliid now controls seven independent swords, accumulates colored engravings, supports allies and predicts formations by mastery. Also includes the Coder (100 functions in 13 languages, scripts and daemons, his rig up to a data center, AI ult and Bitcoin shop), Aegis Zero, Levi, Flash, farming skills and Mod Power. Unified: Einstein, Newton and Marie Curie share 18 equations on five charges; reserve any skill as a trait of the next cast for combos of up to five steps, 36 named signatures and 6 Unifications, ranked by mastery. Vesper and the Rift Gauntlets: pure orbs (5, overload to 9) and Hextech hexorbs open any of 200 dimensions for rift punches, swipes and tears; Shatter, gauntlet breaks and an evolving Hexcore; mastery changes only her planning. Magnus: eleven ranked Slim A appearances, actual calculation previews, compact Alchemist pieces, an ultimate-gated 32,000-unit grid, persistent field armies, cardinal pawns and checkmate planning. Vesper retains every animation pixel while using lossless packed atlases and opt-in per-owner performance timings. Practical grandmaster planning uses observed motion and counterplay; native farming preserves major skills and escape tools; Chess Lab v4 reports damage receipt status. Frieren uses mana, quick and charged Spellcraft (target warned), barriers and targetable party support. Magnus re-plans at most every 0.2 s after a fruitless search. Native farming uses assigned roles and active objective assistance. Gojo uses one authoritative Six Eyes/CE/strain controller, earned Black Flash and one allied Domain guest. Universal team intentions and four persistent athlete game-sense ratings; role-aware farming observations. Creative Herobrine has 45 catalogue entries, HP Tank Steve scaling and paid redstone networks. Frieren/Coder/Dio balance reductions and rooted 75000-range Omen Shadow Step. Objective HP and growth double once per career through a recoverable settings migration. Targetable Stark restores warned ultimate leaps. Callback-local query batching and lossless Frieren atlases preserve combat and animation detail. Round 139: all nine athlete profile values now shape every champion's decisions (reaction, aim, dodging, kiting, holding ultimates, retreating, chasing, waiting for allies, roaming); coach strategy choices are no longer overwritten by the planner; Omen channels stop on taunt, bind and move-block, never land in walls or enemy zones and clear waves with Paranoia; replays and clients agree on athlete profiles; career saves stay bounded. Round 140: the nine athlete profile values only steer movement now (no held or injected casts), with commitment and hysteresis so players stop going back and forth; Steve's recipes have their own cooldowns again; Gojo's domain stuns everyone inside when it opens, with a lighter Infinity and slower Six Eyes; modded champions' extra Mod Power HP is lowered; the editor can apply game-sense rating changes to a career. Round 141: pathing and placement fixes (no freezes at Steve walls, team guidance only when worth it, held strategy settings, Levi flights follow his walk, safe forced moves for Gojo, Coder, Steve, Omen, Gundam, Isliid and Scribble), assist switches in settings.json, and about 17x fewer game-state reads per tick. Raze uses purchased Omen weapons, paid utility, deterministic air strafing and all thirteen pinned athlete attributes; the same Rust core powers Raze Lab v3. Round 142: jungle Levi clears camps again (no roam or regroup points for junglers, stale destinations lapse, camp flights pass the takeoff check, nearest free camp when idle); camp plans keep the coach's wave setting. Round 143: movement assist layers ship switched off (engine pathing as before PR #42, with pathing_redirects diagnostics); Raze gets Omen's buy model with free charges, single-sprite effects, Showstopper into groups, steadier movement, a 155° strafe limit, Mod Power and more damage. Raze balance 0.10.74: free Bucky, protected contextual weapon savings, exactly triple enemy skill damage with unchanged self-damage, and champion follow-up or escape checks. Raze 0.10.75: Attack-scaling physical skills, half-strength air strafing, positional dome launches and champion-count-based 3-12-second landing defence. Raze 0.10.76: Attack-scaling physical skills, half-strength air strafing, positional dome launches, a doubled 56000 satchel radius, true underfoot placement and champion-count-based 3-12-second landing defence.",
